{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he placed him in the house of the roundhouse.</b> This is the pit, and it is a house built into the ground, which they call שיג״א in the vernacular, which has a small opening above through which the prisoners are brought in and through which their light comes. It is from the root of (Genesis 6:16) ״צוהר תעשה לתיבה״, with the interchange of סמ\"ך and צד\"י. And afterwards he explained that it is the house of imprisonment designated for the great ones of the kingdom, which is what it says: ״a place where the king's prisoners were bound.״ For there were two houses of imprisonment there: one for the great ones of the kingdom, great in its light, and one for the rest of the people, small in its light. And what it added and said, ״and he was there in the house of the roundhouse,״ was in order to juxtapose it to ״and YHWH was with Joseph,״ teaching that within the house of imprisonment the Shekhinah was with him." "<b>And it is fitting</b> that the hints also point to the future, and Joseph's affliction in the house of imprisonment is a hint to the exile of Israel, which is likened to a pit. From this they enacted for us in prayer the language of יעלה ויבא, for one who stands in a pit needs to come up from there. And just as the Shekhinah dwells with him inside the prison, so with Israel who dwell in exile the Shekhinah is with them. And just as it is written of Joseph (Psalms 105:18) ״ברזל באה נפשו״, so in the exile of Israel it is written (Psalms 107:10) ״יושבי חשך וצלמות אסירי עני וברזל״. And just as it is written of Joseph ״He inclined kindness to him,״ so Israel in exile is written of them (Ezra 9:9) ״ובעבדותנו לא עזבנו אלהינו ויט עלינו חסד״. And it is written (Isaiah 54:10) ״וחסדי מאתך לא ימוש״. And it is written of Joseph ״and he gave him favor in the eyes of the keeper of the prison,״ so Israel in exile is written of them (Psalms 106:46) ״ויתן אותם לרחמים לפני כל שוביהם״. And just as Joseph came out of the house of prisoners, so Israel are destined to come out of exile and be redeemed, as it is said (Isaiah 49:9) ״לאמר לאסורים צאו״. And just as it is written of Joseph (Psalms 105:19) ״עד עת בא דברו אמרת ה' צרפתהו״, so it is written of the redemption of Israel (Daniel 12:4) ״ואתה דניאל סתום הדברים וחתום הספר עד עת קץ ושוטטו רבים ותרבה הדעת״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:02.757450765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}